alse,"thumb_tiny":"AwAfADCC4iMt/Ko45yT6U5oYYgMoWPuauNAyyyucfO2R9MVWugQV9qeyBasie2Vk3w5z12nvVatCCWPaBuAPvTJNOmaRimzaTkc0MRTo6GrX9m3H+x/31S/2bP8A7H50hmrIpdCAcHsay5Y7ncQyM2TwQM1pyLuxywx/dOKaIcggtJ+LUAUbWxcuGlG1Rzg9TWnUQhwc+bIfbdThGoORnv3oAfRUYiUdCemOtOWMKzEE80Af/9k=","username":""}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"=ska"}]},{"client_msg_id":"fccf4828-cda2-48f7-8862-4e6c5b73f474","type":"message","user":"U776661HA","text":"流石だ...","ts":"1625796355.030500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"IJ2d"}]},{"client_msg_id":"94addc0b-7548-420e-bc81-b48d3abaef3e","type":"message","user":"U03C6TEAZ","text":"gopls は go を差し替える事でできるぽい。 \u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/39619\u003e","ts":"1625796236.030100","attachments":[{"color":"cb2431","fallback":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/39619|#39619 x/tools/gopls: working with the go2go generics prototype\u003e","id":1,"title":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/39619|#39619 x/tools/gopls: working with the go2go generics prototype\u003e","text":"For full context, see \u003chttps://blog.golang.org/generics-next-step|https://blog.golang.org/generics-next-step\u003e.\n\n`gopls` can be made to work with the generics prototype. It will work with any editor that recognizes `.go2` as a Go file extension.\n\nAs of 06/16/2020, the only way to do this is by installing a special version of the VS Code Go extension. This issue will be updated as other editors begin to support this.\n\nFollow these instructions to build and use `gopls` with the \u003chttps://go.googlesource.com/go/+/refs/heads/dev.go2go/README.go2go.md|`dev.go2go`\u003e branch of Go.\n\n*Build `go`*\n\nFirst, build Go at this branch \u003chttps://golang.org/doc/install/source|from source\u003e:\n\n```\ngit clone \u003chttps://go.googlesource.com/go\u003e\ncd go\ngit checkout dev.go2go\n(cd src \u0026amp;\u0026amp; ./make.bash)\n```\n\nMake sure that this version of `go` is first on your PATH. Confirm by running `go version`.  \nNext, using that version of `go`, install the dev.go2go-compatible version of `gopls`:\n\n*Build `gopls`*\n\n```\nGO111MODULE=on go get \u003chttp://golang.org/x/tools/gopls@dev.go2go|golang.org/x/tools/gopls@dev.go2go\u003e \u003chttp://golang.org/x/tools@dev.go2go|golang.org/x/tools@dev.go2go\u003e\n```\n\n*Install a go2-version of the VS Code Go extension*\n\nThe final step will be to configure your editor to recognize `.go2` files. You can do this by installing a special version of the VS Code Go extension that can translate between `.go` and `.go2` files.\n\nThis extension is distributed as a `.vsix` file and can be found in the \u003chttps://github.com/golang/vscode-go/releases/tag/20200722|dev.go2go VS Code Go release\u003e. Download `go-nightly-0.0.0.vsix` and manually install the extension by following these steps:\n\n1. Open a VS Code window and navigate to the Extensions View.\n2. Disable or uninstall the default Go extension. *Note: You will need to undo this when you want to return to your normal development flow.*\n3. Click on the \"...\" in the top-right corner, select \"Install from VSIX...\", and choose `go-nightly-0.0.0.vsix`. Alternatively, you can run code --install-extension path/to/go.vsix or open the Command Palette and run the Extensions: Install from VSIX... command.\n\n*Troubleshooting*\n\nIf it's not working, make sure that your version of Go in VS Code is the dev.go2go version you built.  \nYou can check the version in the `gopls (server)` output logs (View: Toggle Output -\u0026gt; Tasks -\u0026gt; gopls (server)).  \nYou can also explicitly specify the path to the `go version` in your `settings.json` file:\n\n```\n\"go.alternateTools\": {\n \t\"go\": \"/path/to/go/bin/go\"\n}\n```","fields":[{"title":"Labels","value":"Thinking, Tools, gopls","short":true},{"title":"Comments","value":"1","short":true}],"mrkdwn_in":["text"],"blocks":null,"footer":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go|golang/go\u003e","footer_icon":"https://slack.github.com/static/img/favicon-neutral.png","ts":1592343873}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"UV0"}]},{"client_msg_id":"2c17909c-9e53-4188-8bf4-f4c8bcd86591","type":"message","user":"UDDCM376D","text":"つよい","ts":"1625796159.029700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ofkM"}]},{"client_msg_id":"83ae9291-e5ce-40ee-9ebd-2f4323f3e4e3","type":"message","user":"U03C6TEAZ","text":"generics 対応入れてきた。","ts":"1625796098.029300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"uqbn"}]},{"client_msg_id":"4d3ed9be-1e2d-4102-aee9-8d934d0f1e0b","type":"message","user":"U03C6TEAZ","text":"JetBrains すげーな。","ts":"1625796073.029100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"O9TG"}]},{"client_msg_id":"479c50e9-b9d5-4d9d-8847-60f71f2713e6","type":"message","user":"U03C6TEAZ","text":"\u003chttps://blog.jetbrains.com/go/2021/07/08/goland-2021-2-reaches-beta/\u003e","ts":"1625796066.028800","attachments":[{"fallback":"JetBrains Blog: GoLand 2021.2 Reaches Beta! | The GoLand Blog","id":1,"title":"GoLand 2021.2 Reaches Beta! | The GoLand Blog","title_link":"https://blog.jetbrains.com/go/2021/07/08/goland-2021-2-reaches-beta/","text":"GoLand 2021.2 Beta is out! This means that we have stopped adding new features and are now focusing on perfecting the release.  The Beta version is quite stable in comparison to Early Acce","image_url":"https://blog.jetbrains.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Blog_Feature_Image_GoLand.png","blocks":null,"service_name":"JetBrains Blog","service_icon":"https://blog.jetbrains.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/favicon-32x32-1.png","from_url":"https://blog.jetbrains.com/go/2021/07/08/goland-2021-2-reaches-beta/